Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:09.110 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  there is still a lot of unrest and it's  still a very volatile situation here in  afghanistan evidence of that we are  getting reports of some very serious  disturbances in jalalabad now this is a  very important city to the east of kabul  it's towards the border with pakistan uh  it's a very important trading city and  so on and there has been protests there  about the national flag now since we've  seen the arrival of the taliban they  have  gradually been removing afghanistan's  national flag and replacing it with the  taliban flag we have seen that here in  kabul  a lot of people are not happy with that  a lot of people have been very upset  by that but if they have by and large  had to just put up with it in jalalabad  they have not put up with it there has  been resistance to that by a fairly  sizable  part of the community there and we have  seen  uploaded on social media protests in the  streets of people waving the national  flag really quite large protests of  hundreds if not thousands of people and  we do know  that they have put the flag back up  again in an important square in  jalalabad and that there have been  clashes with the taliban with reports of  gunfire and also that a number of people  have been both killed and injured so  that is still developing but it is a  worrying situation and it is it also  comes at a very uh sensitive time here  it is a day before  afghanistan's independence day so  feelings are running high their tensions  are running high and it has resulted in  what we are seeing to be fatal clashes

